      "updated_at": "2026-08-29T12:27:41.324Z",
      "narrative_beats": {
        "beginning": "The narrative opens in the intimate, chiaroscuro-lit dwelling of Abdullah in Makkah, establishing a status quo defined by duty and quiet contemplation. Abdullah prepares for a pivotal trade journey to Syria, while Aminah, in the serene, golden-hued garden of her family home, embodies a patient, dignified anticipation. The inciting incident is the mobilization of the merchant caravan, which disrupts the domestic equilibrium and sets the couple on a path toward inevitable, albeit temporary, separation.",
