        "climax": "The climax occurs not in a grand spectacle, but in the sudden, shattering stillness of the messenger’s arrival at Aminah’s dwelling. The news of Abdullah’s passing in Medina acts as the ultimate turning point, abruptly terminating the hope of his return and forcing a confrontation with the finality of death. This moment is defined by the weight of the messenger’s solemnity and the immediate, visceral shift in Aminah’s world as she processes the irrevocable loss.",
