        "ending": "The story concludes with a final, lingering image of Aminah, whose resilience and grace under sorrow provide a thematic payoff regarding the endurance of the human spirit. The visual tone returns to the soft, flickering light of the oil lamps, grounding the tragedy in a sense of timeless, sacred acceptance. The final resonance is one of quiet strength, leaving the audience with a poignant understanding of the sanctity of the marital bond and the inevitable nature of human departure."
